From 132ab9013c31d45926a37cefc26b43d05c8e3875 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yakyman <246958375+Yakyman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:59:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] layer: Add hide-from-own-screencopy layer rule

Add a boolean layer rule property that omits matching layer surfaces
from wlr-screencopy captures requested by the same Wayland client that
owns the surface. The surface, its pop-ups, shadow and background
effect are simply not rendered into such captures (unlike
block-out-from, which draws a black rectangle), so the capture shows
what lies underneath.

This lets a desktop shell capture the screen to draw a refracting
backdrop behind its own panels without a feedback loop. Captures by
other clients, niri's own screenshots, xdg-desktop-portal screencasts
and normal output rendering are unchanged.

The requesting client is threaded through a new RenderCtx field,
capture_client, set only by the two screencopy render paths; MappedLayer
skips rendering when its rule is set and the client matches. Since the
elements are never produced, hidden surfaces also cause no damage for
that client's copy_with_damage requests.
