 ```
 
+#### `hide-from-own-screencopy`
+
+<sup>Emaki fork</sup>
+
+Set to `true` to omit the surface from wlr-screencopy captures requested by the same Wayland client that owns the surface.
+
+The surface, its pop-ups, its shadow and its background effect are not drawn into such captures at all (unlike `block-out-from`, which draws a black rectangle), so the capture shows whatever is underneath the surface.
+Captures requested by other clients (e.g. grim or OBS), niri's own screenshots, xdg-desktop-portal screencasts and the normal output rendering are not affected.
+
+This is useful for desktop shells that capture the screen to draw a refracting or blurred backdrop behind their own panels, and must not see those panels in the capture.
+
+```kdl
+// Let the Emaki shell capture what is underneath its own panels.
+layer-rule {
+    match namespace="^emaki-"
+
+    hide-from-own-screencopy true
+}
+```
+
 #### `opacity`
 
 Set the opacity of the surface.
